# Integer8 narrowing assignment rejected

Verifies arithmetic promotion does not introduce implicit conversion for plain
assignments, so assigning an int16 value to an int8 variable remains a
compile-time type mismatch.

>>> source
const wide: int16 = 127
const narrow: int8 = wide
print(narrow)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: type mismatch: binding `narrow` expects `int8`, expression produces `int16` at Span { start: 45, end: 49 }

<<< exit
1
